- `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` in this worktree may rerun postinstall steps that dirty generated `packages/happy-wire/dist/*` files or snapshots via line-ending churn. Treat those as verification side effects and revert them unless the story intentionally touches those files.
- Command rows already expose `.cmd-body` as the outer body contract. For layout/animation internals, add nested wrappers such as `.cmd-body-inner` rather than renaming the outer hook.
- Command names are plain text; escape them before using `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for search highlighting. Command descriptions remain trusted operator-authored HTML from `plans/overview-data.js`.
- Progressive CSS animation features should be guarded with `@supports` so native `<details>` behavior remains the fallback path without JS shims.
- Scroll-linked CSS animations that animate non-animation properties (for example toolbar shadow/blur) need an explicit `prefers-reduced-motion` static endpoint; the global guard disables `animation` but does not restore animated property values by itself.
- Hash navigation expands `cmd-<taskId>` rows, centers them with smooth `scrollIntoView`, and applies the shared `cmd-flash` pulse via `flashCommandElement`; in-page jumps should use `navigateToCommand` to preserve that behavior.

